WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.740
Tesla is freeing Texas factory space for cybercab output by winding down cybertruck production around mid-20027. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 657. Shareholder compensation is next, then Shanghai's local content push, then Berlin's waste water milestone, and first principles on shared factory capacity. Gigafactory, Texas, according to the Verge, is the only plant tooled for the cybertruck specialized parts. Elon Musk called the truck the best vehicle

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.520
Tesla has ever made and described the wind down as the end of an era.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:39.120
The model has faced multiple recalls, quality control issues, and price revisions since

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.600
its 2023 launch as a rival to trucks from Ford and General Motors.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:51.080
Deliveries in the third quarter fell to 4,323 from 12,364 in the second quarter.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:57.480
Sales estimates show roughly 70,000 units delivered cumulatively through September 2026.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:02.920
Cybertruck Lead Engineer Wes Morrill said the truck was an incredible technology development

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:08.420
platform that lives on through CyberCab, which has butterfly doors and no steering wheel,

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:13.700
pedals or mirrors. Musk has not specified whether production will move elsewhere or end

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:19.745
entirely. Tesla shareholders Startup Fortune reported approved a compensation package

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:25.585
for Elon Musk that could reach $1 trillion. Shanghai's plant, according to CNEV Post,

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:31.665
now has parts localization at 98%. That higher rate allows joint developments with

00:01:31.665 --> 00:01:37.323
Chinese suppliers to be exported globally. Giga Berlin, Drive Tesla Canada reported,

00:01:37.943 --> 00:01:42.823
marked two years without discharging process wastewater after recycling 465

00:01:42.823 --> 00:01:47.963
million liters. IMC logistics received the first vehicle from its order of 50

00:01:47.963 --> 00:01:53.063
Tesla semis. Canadian backed Eku Energy commissioned a 500 megawatt hour

00:01:53.063 --> 00:01:55.103
Megapack installation in Canberra.

00:01:55.743 --> 00:02:00.503
Giga, Texas, Tesla Roddy reported, shifted to round-the-clock vehicle production through

00:02:00.503 --> 00:02:02.203
the end of 2026.

00:02:02.743 --> 00:02:09.443
Williamsdale, according to Basinor, added a 250-megawatt Tesla Megapack farm at a cost of $150

00:02:09.443 --> 00:02:09.963
million.

00:02:10.783 --> 00:02:16.183
Agility Robotics, Investors Business Daily reported, began public trading following its

00:02:16.183 --> 00:02:19.183
special-purpose acquisition company, or SPAC, merger.

00:02:19.883 --> 00:02:24.143
automakers, according to electric vehicles, will face congressional hearings on tariffs

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:26.763
and robotaxi oversight under the new Congress.

00:02:27.383 --> 00:02:33.743
A German survey, Carbuzz reported, ranked Tesla last among 30 brands, and TUV named the

00:02:33.743 --> 00:02:35.783
Model Y the least reliable vehicle.

00:02:36.443 --> 00:02:41.223
Drone footage on Reddit's Tesla Motors community showed the Optimus factory at Giga, Texas

00:02:41.223 --> 00:02:47.983
at roughly 55% steel completion, with limited production still targeted for the end of 2027.

00:02:47.983 --> 00:02:54.083
7. Cybercabs in Detroit, a Detroit-free press post showed, joined Waymo vehicles for Michigan

00:02:54.083 --> 00:02:59.863
weather testing. Elsewhere, Tesla will open its first store in Argentina this month, Drive

00:02:59.863 --> 00:03:05.523
Tesla Canada reported. The Globe and Mail compared Tesla and BYD on charging infrastructure

00:03:05.523 --> 00:03:11.023
strength. A survey found municipal permitting delays are slowing electric vehicle or EV

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:16.563
charger rollout in Canada. Tesla replied to National Highway Traffic Safety Administration,

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:22.523
or NHTSA, questions on cybercab certification, but kept the answers confidential.

00:03:23.183 --> 00:03:27.823
The Roadster Kickflip demonstration uses 10 nozzles and provides no rider data.

00:03:28.363 --> 00:03:33.203
That Kickflip is shown uncrewed with a 0.81 second 0-60 time.

00:03:33.803 --> 00:03:39.203
And full self-driving, or FSD, tests produce the reaction, oh my gosh, this is scary.

00:03:39.923 --> 00:03:43.123
A point of view video shows the Roadster performing a Kickflip.

00:03:43.123 --> 00:03:47.363
Tesla is approaching humanoid robot sales with one remaining constraint.

00:03:47.923 --> 00:03:51.623
Tesla owners can now submit and vote on software feature requests.

00:03:52.203 --> 00:03:56.063
Tesla's active robot taxi markets now spend seven U.S. regions.

00:03:56.823 --> 00:04:00.503
Optimus production at 20,000 robots per week remains a year away.

00:04:01.083 --> 00:04:04.983
Powerwall three replacement details after one year are now confirmed.

00:04:05.663 --> 00:04:08.843
Deepways Electric Semi reached New Zealand under a new name.

00:04:08.843 --> 00:04:16.076
The remaining constraint is not floor space, but the rate at which new processes can be validated and handed to operations.

00:04:16.896 --> 00:04:24.496
Distributing manufacturing risk across continents while tightening local content is the through line, not a dedicated line for every product.

00:04:25.176 --> 00:04:35.376
Nearly every Shanghai component either originates inside China or is produced by joint ventures Tesla Connectsport, which shortens the distance between a design change and the production line.

00:04:35.376 --> 00:04:39.096
Energy products can scale without waiting for vehicle volume.

00:04:39.676 --> 00:04:45.916
Recycling process water removes one regulatory variable from future expansion decisions in water-stressed regions.

00:04:46.416 --> 00:04:51.976
Those moves reduce single-site exposure and create optionality for both vehicle and energy programs.

00:04:52.596 --> 00:04:57.956
Capital already committed to these sites now earns returns across multiple product lines rather than one.

00:04:58.596 --> 00:05:03.696
Continuous shifts raise how many vehicles and energy products can leave a site without adding floor space.

00:05:03.696 --> 00:05:09.256
A live commercial truck data set on duty cycle, charging windows, and payload economics

00:05:09.256 --> 00:05:11.076
now sits on shared infrastructure.

00:05:11.616 --> 00:05:16.776
Any improvement in cell yield or pack assembly benefits vehicles, energy storage, and future

00:05:16.776 --> 00:05:17.716
robots at once.

00:05:18.376 --> 00:05:23.436
That overlap lowers the marginal cost of each new program once the base processes are stable.

00:05:24.076 --> 00:05:29.236
When localization, energy projects, and round-the-clock shifts advance together, the company

00:05:29.236 --> 00:05:32.896
is converting fixed assets into variable output across categories.

00:05:33.576 --> 00:05:38.096
Each additional validated process multiplies the return on the capital already spent.

00:05:38.656 --> 00:05:43.196
Before we go, tomorrow I'll be tracking whether more cybercabs show up in winter testing

00:05:43.196 --> 00:05:45.076
beside other Robotaxi fleets.

